\tag{fdip}
\title{The two constructive limits}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{The [finite laws](fdip-00HX) retain a physical boundary while the
number of field values grows. Their first continuum limit keeps that
boundary fixed; removing the boundary is a second limit. Which
continuum state do these successive limits select, and what regularity
does it retain?}

